  "practice": [
    "Say ই three times with a short, relaxed sound: i, i, i.",
    "Read each vocabulary word aloud and listen for ই at the beginning.",
    "Contrast ই (i) with আ (a): ইট (iṭ), আম (am).",
    "Write ই five times, paying attention to its curved left side and top line."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ই is the third independent vowel in the Bengali alphabet. It has a short i sound similar to the vowel in “sit.”",
    "When ই follows a consonant, it becomes the vowel mark ি (ই-কার): ক + ি = কি (ki). Although ি is written to the left of the consonant, it is pronounced after it.",
    "Keep ই distinct from the longer ঈ sound in careful spelling. In modern Bengali speech, ই and ঈ are often pronounced alike, but their written forms remain different."
  ]
